{"title":"Career roadmap · NGO Program Officer","role":"NGO Program Officer","summary":"An NGO Program Officer plans, coordinates, implements, monitors and reports social-development programmes such as education, healthcare, livelihoods, women and child development, rural development, disability inclusion, youth development and community empowerment.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1","Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Social Work (BSW)"},"about":[{"label":"Alignment","text":"Strong direct alignment"}],"intro":[{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"A BSW can provide a direct entry route into NGO programme, fieldwork and community-development roles. Larger programme-management roles often require relevant experience and sometimes an MSW/MPP/Development Studies qualification."}]}],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Typical route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["BSW","NGO/Community Development Internship","Fieldwork/Project Assistant","Programme Associate","Programme Officer","Senior Programme Officer","Programme Manager","Programme Lead","Programme Director"]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build social-work fundamentals, fieldwork experience, community engagement, documentation and monitoring skills."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Specialise in a development area such as education, health, livelihoods, women & children, rural development or youth programmes."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Move into programme management, partnerships, monitoring & evaluation, grants or impact strategy."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Progress toward Programme Director, State/Regional Programme Head, Development Consultant, CSR/Impact Lead or senior development-sector leadership."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of pr